      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Prioritizing proximity to transit hubs should serve as the foundation principle to ensure equity in your housing mandate. Modern urban planning underscores the importance of accessible public transit as a means to access jobs, education, and healthcare, which can significantly impact residents' quality of life. By doing so, the city can eventually reduce inequity in service and opportunity, and support environmental goals by promoting public transportation over personal vehicle dependency. This approach should be clear and measurable so that all stakeholders can understand how the fruits of the mandate will be equitably distributed.",
      "source": "target",
